    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d436">

                <pb facs="0335" n="331" xml:id="pg331"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1163P92/100: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Tsingtao</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gourley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tsingtao</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-05-26T17:00:00+08:00">May 26, 1938—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 26—9:28 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My May 25, 2 p.m., and May 25, 8 p.m.<anchor n="26" xml:id="d436-f1"/> American
                    Presbyterian Mission in Tsingtao ordered all refugees to leave school compound
                    and notified Japanese that order had been given. Relatives of suspected man have
                    already left.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Hankow, Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gourley</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d436-f1" n="26" xml:id="d436-f1-content">
                <p>Neither printed; see Department’s reply, May 25, 9 p.m., <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >supra.</hi></p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
